+# Item priority
+
+**Go:** go, existing items are normal (2026-10-12)
+
+## Intent
+
+The owner: "Items should have a priority, and I want to filter the list to one priority." High and
+low items should stand out in the list, and a filter shows just one priority.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Priorities are high, normal and low, and existing items get normal: every item then has a
+  priority and the filter never hides an item for having none; rejected: no priority until set
+  (owner, 2026-10-12)
+- Only high and low are shown next to a title, so the usual case stays quiet; rejected: a label on
+  every item (owner, 2026-10-12)
+
+## Acceptance items
+
+- **AC-1** A migration adds a priority to items (high, normal or low, nothing else), and every
+  existing item gets normal.
+- **AC-2** A high or low item shows its priority after its title ("— high", "— low"); normal items
+  show none.
+- **AC-3** `/?priority=<high|normal|low>` lists only the items of that priority, in id order.
+- **AC-4** `/` lists all items in id order, as before.
+- **AC-5** Every view shows the filters All, High, Normal and Low, and the current one is not a
+  link.
+- **AC-6** Any other `priority` value must answer 400 and list nothing.
+- **AC-7** A priority filter that matches nothing says "No high-priority items." (or normal, low);
+  an empty table says "No items yet." in every view.
+- **AC-8** `/?priority=high` is listed in `traffic/routes.json`, so synthetic traffic exercises it.
+
+## Core flow
+
+1. Open the list: every item, high and low ones labelled.
+2. Follow "High": just the high-priority items.
+3. Follow "All": back to every item.
+
+## States
+
+| State          | List shows             | Message                 | Current filter |
+| -------------- | ---------------------- | ----------------------- | -------------- |
+| All priorities | every item             | none                    | All            |
+| One priority   | items of that priority | none                    | that priority  |
+| No match       | nothing                | No high-priority items. | that priority  |
+| Empty table    | nothing                | No items yet.           | any            |
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Setting an item's priority from the page: there is no write route yet.
+- Sorting by priority.
